// Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded two-argument arc tangent of F64
//
// atan2(y, x) is a quadrant offset (0, +-pi/2 or +-pi) plus or minus atan(z),
// z = min(|x|, |y|) / max(|x|, |y|), and atan(z) = atan(j/64) +
// atan((z - j/64) / (1 + z j/64)) with a short odd polynomial. A second F64
// stage in double-double takes most of what the first can't round. The rest,
// and inputs whose exponents differ by 53 or more, go to an accurate path that
// evaluates a degree-29/29 rational approximation of atan in 192-bit "tint"
// arithmetic. Round to nearest only. Zeros and infinities follow C99. A NaN
// comes back quiet, y's if both are NaN (as x86's y + x).
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/atan2/atan2.c and tint.h via RazorForge's
// B64Atan2.rf.
// Copyright (c) 2024-2025 Paul Zimmermann and Alexei Sibidanov (atan2.c)
// Copyright (c) 2023-2024 Paul Zimmermann and Alexei Sibidanov (tint.h)
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

